{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls","id":625646,"title":"Help me build my Orthodox LS !","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-13T10:04:24-07:00","id":625646,"title":"Help me build my Orthodox LS !","content":"Hi folks,<br /> <br /> Please first let me introduce you to the setting, which happens to take place in a fictive version of K\u00f6nigsberg/Kaliningrad in northern eastern Europe. My goal here is to create an alternative place that would act as a melting pot of whatever i find interesting for a dark, oppressed and coercitive story taking place in an eastern Europe city.<br /> <br /> The population is a third German, a third local (Baltic and Polish population) and a third Russian.<br /> <br /> Being fictive, you can find in the city : a jewish ghetto and its golem story, some Ukrainian refugees and a large slave market, a powerful Russian mafia, a new group of extremely rich people who got fortunate after 1991, an old Prussian mood that seems haunted by romantic and death ideologies, and, of course, a very large orthodox Church currently building 5 new churches in town.<br /> The mood might go from Kronenbergs\u2019s \u201cEastern Promises\u201d to the episodes of Urasawa\u2019s \u201cMonster\u201d to Eisenstein's masterpiece \u201cIvan Grozny\u201d.<br /> <br /> We all agree that the Lancea Sanctum is, whatever the 2nd edition settings says, heavily bound to the Catholic Church. Now I love the Catholics settings, but I want something different here, I want a scary, dark, mystical and illuminated orthodox Church. I want a Church that believes in millenarianism and in the holy Russian soul, a Church ruled by hairy popes kissing golden icons in the smell of cloudy encens.<br /> <br /> Now, my bishop, which I recall a Starets, is a scary illuminated Nosferatu which looks like the historical Rasputin. His name, Theraponte, is taken from a side character of Dostoievski\u2019s Karamazov, a monk full of hate and disgust for life, that also have personal daily relationships with demon entities (no shit, it's in the book !)<br /> <br /> As I want orthodoxy to be at the center of my kindred setting, how do I organise my LS ? Do i just copy paste the catholic one, changing names ? Is there any outlet, books or extra setting in the WoD for this kind of questions ? some other RPG ? Any metaplot in sight ? Kindred patriarchs background ?<br /> <br /> Obviously i won't get my players to attempt midnight masse, even if one of them has his character coming from an old odd monastery that works as an orphanage.<br /> My group also contains a esoteric bounty hunter in the search for some old religious treasures.<br /> The LS has always been the most obscure and undefined covenant in Requiem in my eyes (understand here that the problem is on my side, i just don't get that covenant as good as i get the others), and thus makes it especially hard to adapt.<br /> <br /> Do you guys have any advice, tips, database, movies or literature to share with me ? Basically i understand that i will have to work this from scratch, so any inspirational stuff or good ideas is very welcome here !<br /> <br /> Thanks !<br /> <br /> <br /> PS : i am not allowed to upload picture attachments; but i would like to share the visual stuff that i used to that point with you. Is there a way ?<br /> PPS : as english is not my native tongue, i hope all i speak here is understandable ! thanks for reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","user":"essen_ko","date":". 08-13-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:39:17-07:00","id":626627,"title":"","content":"So, Russian Orthodox Church. <br /> <br /> The first thing I want to say is that, despite being heavily Catholic influenced, there are plenty of ways of portraying the LS as anything but Catholic. The core of the Church is the Testament of Longinus (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62830/The-Testament-of-Longinus\" target=\"_blank\">which is a good read if you get it</a>). <br /> <br /> All in all, while there's a lot of details that are different between Catholics and Orthodoxes, most of those details will generally be lost when translated to vampire-hood. Orthodox, from the sounds of it, are less hung up on marriage, so that general stance of horror may be better. There's no standard for a Eucharist in the Lancea et Sanctum - there's no real standard for how Midnight Mass runs at all, in fact, so pretty much every city has the potential to be different. There's no Pope, only regional churches, so the default LeS is similar to the Orthodox church in this instance. <br /> <br /> The idea of the Original Sin promenant in Catholicism doesn't apply to vampires - you're damned by your own actions. But, overall, this major difference in cannon for the living really doesn't quite apply to the vampires. At best, an Orthodox LeS might not talk about vampires being Damned, but they still have a divine purpose to fulfill in the world.<br /> <br /> Mary doesn't apply to vampires either, though there is the Livian Heresy, which may still make an appearance in the Orthodox version.<br /> <br /> A large aspect of the Orthodox church is redemption through Good Works instead of the Faith Alone doctrine of the Catholic Church. This means that the LeS would put greater emphasis on hunting sinners and living as holy monsters for earning God's eyes approval. <br /> <br /> There are several different doctrines that differ on the question of what happens when a vampire dies - do they go to rule in Hell, or do they go to Heaven? It often switches, depending on individual games. That's one that'll have to be answered for your church individually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:45:49-07:00","id":626633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls#post625646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS : i am not allowed to upload picture attachments; but i would like to share the visual stuff that i used to that point with you. Is there a way ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Upload a picture to google+ or some other website, then give us a link. Something like this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i3.photobucket.com/albums/y75/majere62/soeurmarie.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Nun of the Machine</a><br /> Or just paste the url - <a href=\"http://940ee6dce6677fa01d25-0f55c9129972ac85d6b1f4e703468e6b.r99.cf2.rackcdn.com/products/pictures/203938.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://940ee6dce6677fa01d25-0f55c912...res/203938.jpg</a> (this is the childer of the Plague Angel, read a bit about her in the Mekhet book)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PPS : as english is not my native tongue, i hope all i speak here is understandable ! thanks for reading. </div> </div> </div>Its perfect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T07:19:55-07:00","id":628588,"title":"","content":"From which i recall from your advices and ideas, there\u2019s to define the \u201cboard\u201d of Kindred morality.<br /> <br /> Russian Orthodox, that\u2019s a nice point you underline here (considering other Patriarchas influences)<br /> <br /> I am so considering conflicting three religious mortal conspirations under the single rule of the local LeS. The Patriarch stands upon theological conclaves and faithful vendettas, earning his assets from internal conflicts.<br /> A fanstamagoric Nosferatu could take benefits from the rivalry between the Czech Jewish diaspora, the Russian linked orthodoxes and the churches build with the Byzantin Patriarch\u2019s money.<br /> The LeS enlarge it self to a multi cultural covenant build by the Kindred taking benefits of the local religious rivalry.<br /> <br /> That hand though, perfectly terrifying. How could one doubt such a gesture :<br /> <a href=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20140903123745/assassinscreed/images/0/0e/Grigori_Rasputin.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb2...i_Rasputin.jpg</a><br /> <a href=\"https://vatopaidi.files.wordpress.com/2010/03/serge-chevitch-biographie-4.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://vatopaidi.files.wordpress.co...ographie-4.jpg</a><br /> <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Rasputin-Germogen-Iliodor.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikiped...en-Iliodor.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <br /> As DamnationCity says : &quot;Knock yourselves out, Storytellers; they're your tools now.&quot;<br /> I will further post when more advanced.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your words btw !<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T15:50:58-07:00","id":629130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=628588#post628588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so considering conflicting three religious mortal conspirations under the single rule of the local LeS. The Patriarch stands upon theological conclaves and faithful vendettas, earning his assets from internal conflicts.<br /> A fanstamagoric Nosferatu could take benefits from the rivalry between the Czech Jewish diaspora, the Russian linked orthodoxes and the churches build with the Byzantin Patriarch\u2019s money.<br /> The LeS enlarge it self to a multi cultural covenant build by the Kindred taking benefits of the local religious rivalry</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite different from the way the L&amp;S has been portrayed lately. I would expect there to be covenants linked to Orthodox churches outside the L&amp;S. Typically, the L&amp;S presence in your city might be a minority from from Germany or another western country. Still, this sounds interesting and certainly colourful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T13:32:48-07:00","id":631494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=629130#post629130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's quite different from the way the L&amp;S has been portrayed lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not own the LS order book (but it's quite old anyway). You mean 2nd corebook ?<br /> And do you suggest here that the local LS shall be linked to one specific human group, and dominate the others through ?<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a nice idea you got : a Lutheran church as the shelter of german nationalistic interests and rests of old fashioned ideologies. (not to forget that Kaliningrad sits on the east side of the Danzig canal !)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:44:18-07:00","id":631567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=631494#post631494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not own the LS order book (but it's quite old anyway). You mean 2nd corebook ?<br /> And do you suggest here that the local LS shall be linked to one specific human group, and dominate the others through ?<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a nice idea you got : a Lutheran church as the shelter of german nationalistic interests and rests of old fashioned ideologies. (not to forget that Kaliningrad sits on the east side of the Danzig canal !)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Athens section of the corebook has a three thousand year old religion that believes in both Apollo and God and in harassing kine for some reason, while the the last representative of the Lancea et Sanctum came from a Turkish &quot;Sultanate&quot;. And <i>Dark Eras</i> had about three cults connected to either Catholicism or Islam, but not the L&amp;S. So I've interpreted that to mean that a local Christian tradition doesn't necessarily translate to a local L&amp;S tradition. I don't recall hearing much about them in Eastern Europe anyway. Not that it couldn't be done really well; there's just room for other covenants, a bit like how the Tismanu and Vedma bloodlines were both in the Ordo Dracul book, rather than the L&amp;S and CotC respectively, which would be more obvious.<br /> <br /> I was thinking more of a pseudo-Catholic L&amp;S that supported the Teutonic Order and that still struggles against Lithuanian heathens (not so much in Kaliningrad obviously, but maybe a little). But then I didn't know that Lutheranism actually spread east across Prussia, so that might work too.<br /> <br /> By the way, I haven't noticed if anyone but me types &quot;L&amp;S&quot;, but it so reminds me of M&amp;S.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T07:29:12-07:00","id":632228,"title":"","content":"So basically LS is always a big homebrew of whatever cultural believes you fell like putting into i presume. \u200bDamnation City made it a bit to segregate with its social schemes opposing religion and politics. <br /> There's also some to dig from the central european jewish community, Praag being the capital. I mean, there must be some sort of Kindred heritage from the time before Christ. As the last books of the Bible didn't write themselves up ( focusing on the Books of the Maccabees which were written arround 150BC), a pre-Longinus Kindred culture could exists. But i feel very ignorant here since i neither have read the Longinus Testament yet (ordering it) neither Rome (next year i hope). <br /> Cain and Lilith are still two kindred mythological figures which, as all of us i guess, im attached to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As you mention it, the Teutonic order could still somewhat be willing to take revanche from the battle of Grunewald/Tanenberg (from whatever side you choose to tell the story). Btw, it occurs that Baltic people even now, strongly still consider themselves as non-religious folks (which is very specific to these regions and some scandinavians) So Pagans to the Circle of the Crone, obviously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=631567#post631567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way, I haven't noticed if anyone but me types &quot;L&amp;S&quot;, but it so reminds me of M&amp;S.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T11:58:25-07:00","id":632568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=632228#post632228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically LS is always a big homebrew of whatever cultural believes you fell like putting into i presume. \u200bDamnation City made it a bit to segregate with its social schemes opposing religion and politics.<br /> There's also some to dig from the central european jewish community, Praag being the capital. I mean, there must be some sort of Kindred heritage from the time before Christ. As the last books of the Bible didn't write themselves up ( focusing on the Books of the Maccabees which were written arround 150BC), a pre-Longinus Kindred culture could exists. But i feel very ignorant here since i neither have read the Longinus Testament yet (ordering it) neither Rome (next year i hope).<br /> Cain and Lilith are still two kindred mythological figures which, as all of us i guess, im attached to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As you mention it, the Teutonic order could still somewhat be willing to take revanche from the battle of Grunewald/Tanenberg (from whatever side you choose to tell the story). Btw, it occurs that Baltic people even now, strongly still consider themselves as non-religious folks (which is very specific to these regions and some scandinavians) So Pagans to the Circle of the Crone, obviously.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any covenant can be tweaked to improve your setting. Personally, I like the Lancea et Sanctum to be distinct from all Christian sects, but typically adopting their customs due its lack of centralisation and the fact that most of its members' see it from perspectives based on their mortal understanding. So even an atheist turned spear will believe in some ideas that he knew of from whatever related faith is familiar to him, whether it's described in the Testament of Longinus or not.<br /> <br /> It is said that the L&amp;S less relevant in less religious cities. I suppose a way around that would be to make the covenant appealing to irreligious neonates. Less talk of spiritual rewards, obligations to God and futile rituals, more material rewards and connections. That's essentially Invictus with Theban sorcery, which would normally suggest that Invictus themselves aren't there. Perhaps Carthians overthrew them while the L&amp;S either stood aside or helped? Although I feel like the Ordo Dracul could be a good fit for that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> M&amp;S (Marks and Spencer) is a British retail chain that sells upmarket groceries and clothes, as opposed to a religion dedicated to making humanity suffer to keep them on the straight and narrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T21:17:56-07:00","id":634232,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Lancea et Sanctum predates the split between the eastern and western churches by a considerable margin, and that (as I recall) the Eastern Roman Empire was a major center of the Sanctified before and (especially) after the fall of Rome. Eastern kindred are likely just as steeped in the trappings of the Orthodox Church(es) as western kindred are in those of Catholicism (and, to an extent, Protestantism). That said, the Lance in Russia certainly wouldn't use a Latin name.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole &quot;salvation by faith alone&quot; like is a <i>P</i><i>rotestant </i>thing; Catholics, as I understand it, still affirm the importance of Good Works.<br /> <br /> The point about the Sanctified being distinct from living branches of Christianity is a good one; I imagine that most Christians, with the exception of real fire-and-brimstone types, won't be very comfortable with the teachings of the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> What makes the Sanctum work, in my mind, is the sheer hopelessness and futility of the kindred condition. As a vampire, you are going to hurt people all the time. You are occasionally going to lose control and kill people. You will be rejected by and/or outlive everyone you care about, unless you're reduced to ash before that point. Once the reality of that sinks in, I can see how the idea that, even as a monster, you're still part of God's plan, would become more attractive. It's a sect that <i>makes sense</i> for vampires, and doesn't really for mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 08-21-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T05:32:51-07:00","id":634471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634232#post634232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the whole &quot;salvation by faith alone&quot; like is a <i>P</i><i>rotestant </i>thing; Catholics, as I understand it, still affirm the importance of Good Works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Former Roman (as in &quot;literally living in Rome&quot; ohooh me so funny) Catholic here. This is indeed true. In Catholicism, you are saved by faith, but being faithful means that you are actually <i>working </i>towards it, one way or another. So, it's both, actually.<br /> <br /> The differences between the Orthodox and the Catholic Curch wouldn't matter <i>to a vampire in the Lancea</i>.<br /> The Orthodox Church doesn't believe in the moral consequences of the Original Sin, in the infallibility of the Pope (of course). There are also, obviously, differences in the rites. And there is no celibacy for the clergy. That's it. Nothing major for a vampire... really major stuff for a theologist.<br /> <br /> The Lancea is neither Catholic nor Protestant nor everything else. Ok, it <i>smells </i>of Catholicism, but it's not. The Lancea is the Lancea. It has its corpus of holy scriptures, it has its own rites, etcetera. There is no central &quot;political&quot; religious figure, so they don't have someone to actually choose what is canon, or how a clergyman or a layman has to act. The doctrine of salvation by faith was probably thrown out of a window by virtue of, you know, not being really applicable to the damned. It's kinda difficult being saved by faith when you are a vampire. <i>This</i> could be an important issue in the Lancea, however, but not really mattering to the OP. Your Lancea will have <i>the trappings</i> of what your Bishop (or whatever they will call themselves) believes in. I expect there'd be lots of heresies (and political infighting).<br /> <br /> Maybe the Mass could be different in a mainly Orthodox country. You will probably see more bearded clergymen,with a need to bless <i>everything</i>. This could be a stereotype (as I've never met a non-Catholic Christian), but I've seen lots of photos of Orthodox priests blessing whatever. Cars. Rifles. Tanks.<br /> I mean, in Italy (at least) we have priests going door to door wanting to bless your house (... ok, now that I think of it, Lancea vampires blessing Havens, this is nice). But a strong Lancea &quot;asking&quot; to bless every business co-opted by the Invictus? Plot Point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T08:07:09-07:00","id":634608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634232#post634232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the Lance in Russia certainly wouldn't use a Latin name.<br /> <br /> Once the reality of that sinks in, I can see how the idea that, even as a monster, you're still part of God's plan, would become more attractive. It's a sect that <i>makes sense</i> for vampires, and doesn't really for mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, you got two good points over there. <br /> The religious center of the roman world has always been in the east, saying, in Greece. From pagan Gods, to Paul's travels, to Nicea Council, Eagan sea is the cradle of both old and new religions in the western world (ok, this is a troll, but let say eastern mediterranean ) . Therefor the name shall be in greek (or greek Byzantin).<br /> <br /> Also I like the way you highlight the Kindred morality problem. Gives me idea ! Actually, for a helpless vampire who fell down to 3 dots in Humanity because of accumulation of mistakes and free atrocity, the crossing of the god-machine angels (which are very real) could mean moral salvation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SNESferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634471#post634471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> You will probably see more bearded clergymen,with a need to bless <i>everything</i>. This could be a stereotype (as I've never met a non-Catholic Christian), but I've seen lots of photos of Orthodox priests blessing whatever. Cars. Rifles. Tanks.<br /> I mean, in Italy (at least) we have priests going door to door wanting to bless your house (... ok, now that I think of it, Lancea vampires blessing Havens, this is nice). But a strong Lancea &quot;asking&quot; to bless every business co-opted by the Invictus? Plot Point.</div> </div> </div> </div> First, it is true that the distinction between east and west is not to be found on the theological side here, as you wisely underline. Even tough, Pope infaibility (which is a doctrine whom rised pretty late in History, somewhen between the Ve and et XIe century) could be an important question if a sanctified gets really attached to the catholic heritage of the L&amp;S (after all, there must be at least a couple powerful kindred in Rome taking advantage of the Pope's spiritual power)<br /> <br /> You point the finger on something brilliant sir, blessings, to bless everything, like fields and cows in the middle ages. After all, this game is about neo-feodality, so why not bringing it further ?<br /> Neonates don't have to believe in God or in Longinus to be submitted to the local tradition. So, as you suggest, the prince could use the the LS to overlook it's subjects, and control somewhat their everynight lifes.<br /> Also, it gives LS power, which is what it lacked in my eyes. LS shall be powerful if you want it or not, that's what makes it scary, its the spiritual authority of the Kindred, the second Estate, and then it also holds some temporal too. Personnel believes and spirituality come second.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6461-essen_ko","name":"essen_ko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:20:12-07:00","id":634871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=631494#post631494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not own the LS order book (but it's quite old anyway). You mean 2nd corebook ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically the 2nd, but its been hinted at being different in a number of books. I actually recommend against getting any of the old covenant books - they're outdated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=632228#post632228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically LS is always a big homebrew of whatever cultural believes you fell like putting into i presume.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. The local bishop makes all the rules, based on his interpretation of the Testament.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But i feel very ignorant here since i neither have read the Longinus Testament yet (ordering it) neither Rome (next year i hope).<br /> Cain and Lilith are still two kindred mythological figures which, as all of us i guess, im attached to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div> Requiem for Rome isn't really a big deal. It shows the Lance as plucky underdogs of Rome society, but doesn't really help. While the Cannite Heresy does have its roots here, its specifically made up by some vampire who's looking into manipulating the mortals - its not an actual Kindred legend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Pagans to the Circle of the Crone, obviously. </div> </div> </div> Just a note - the Circle of the Crone is heavily Neo-Pagan / Wicca themed. Its going to need as much of a local revision as the LS, maybe more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=632568#post632568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is said that the L&amp;S less relevant in less religious cities. I suppose a way around that would be to make the covenant appealing to irreligious neonates. Less talk of spiritual rewards, obligations to God and futile rituals, more material rewards and connections. That's essentially Invictus with Theban sorcery, which would normally suggest that Invictus themselves aren't there. Perhaps Carthians overthrew them while the L&amp;S either stood aside or helped? Although I feel like the Ordo Dracul could be a good fit for that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> The LeS actually has a Creed for those who don't believe in God, but still practice the philosophy and Theban Sorceries. The Lance is alone among Kindred covenants in that it makes a very heavy suggestion that its adherants focus on feeding upon the morally weak of the herd (ie sinners and criminals), which is actually very appealing to someone looking for purpose in unlife.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634232#post634232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the whole &quot;salvation by faith alone&quot; like is a <i>P</i><i>rotestant </i>thing; Catholics, as I understand it, still affirm the importance of Good Works.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ish? I mean, Good Works are important, but Faith is considered more important by the vast majority. You can be a shit person, then repent on your deathbed, and still be saved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point about the Sanctified being distinct from living branches of Christianity is a good one; I imagine that most Christians, with the exception of real fire-and-brimstone types, won't be very comfortable with the teachings of the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> What makes the Sanctum work, in my mind, is the sheer hopelessness and futility of the kindred condition. As a vampire, you are going to hurt people all the time. You are occasionally going to lose control and kill people. You will be rejected by and/or outlive everyone you care about, unless you're reduced to ash before that point. Once the reality of that sinks in, I can see how the idea that, even as a monster, you're still part of God's plan, would become more attractive. It's a sect that <i>makes sense</i> for vampires, and doesn't really for mortals. </div> </div> </div> Agreed. But then, that's why joining a covenant is a breaking point - you're not thinking like a living person anymore. And, to be honest, that divine monster role is actually pretty appealing. You can still make the world a better place, despite being a predator that ruins almost anything you touch.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SNESferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634471#post634471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea is neither Catholic nor Protestant nor everything else. Ok, it <i>smells </i>of Catholicism, but it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, but the talk of Catholic versus Protestant brought something to mind. I do want to say something about Livia and the Livian Heresies. The Lance has... issues with flirting with divine female figures. Where the Catholic Church reveres Mary as the Queen of Heaven (perhaps a nod to some local beliefs that the Church absorbed), Proestants do not. So, in this case, the Lance is a bit less Catholic-like, and more Protestant-like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The doctrine of salvation by faith was probably thrown out of a window by virtue of, you know, not being really applicable to the damned. </div> </div> </div>Not to mention being bad for games. Good Works is a lot more active, which is better for stories!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe the Mass could be different in a mainly Orthodox country. You will probably see more bearded clergymen,with a need to bless <i>everything</i>. This could be a stereotype (as I've never met a non-Catholic Christian), but I've seen lots of photos of Orthodox priests blessing whatever. Cars. Rifles. Tanks.<br /> I mean, in Italy (at least) we have priests going door to door wanting to bless your house (... ok, now that I think of it, Lancea vampires blessing Havens, this is nice). But a strong Lancea &quot;asking&quot; to bless every business co-opted by the Invictus? Plot Point. </div> </div> </div>Neat, I like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>essen_ko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634608#post634608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I like the way you highlight the Kindred morality problem. Gives me idea ! Actually, for a helpless vampire who fell down to 3 dots in Humanity because of accumulation of mistakes and free atrocity, the crossing of the god-machine angels (which are very real) could mean moral salvation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Keep in mind that, to learn Theban, you need to maintain around Humanity 5 or so. So, the Chruch absolutely wants to pull you out of that low Humanity spiral for their own selfish reasons. Its ironic, in a way, that the Lancea et Sanctum encourages its members to be the most human (and bane-filled), when they're one of the most monstrous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, it is true that the distinction between east and west is not to be found on the theological side here, as you wisely underline. Even tough, Pope infaibility (which is a doctrine whom rised pretty late in History, somewhen between the Ve and et XIe century) could be an important question if a sanctified gets really attached to the catholic heritage of the L&amp;S (after all, there must be at least a couple powerful kindred in Rome taking advantage of the Pope's spiritual power) </div> </div> </div> Papal infailibilty has to be invoked to work, its not constant. So, its easily explained away by the times its invoked, they're not being manipulated. Othertimes, its free game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T12:06:27-07:00","id":634928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634871#post634871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 1. The LeS actually has a Creed for those who don't believe in God, but still practice the philosophy and Theban Sorceries. The Lance is alone among Kindred covenants in that it makes a very heavy suggestion that its adherants focus on feeding upon the morally weak of the herd (ie sinners and criminals), which is actually very appealing to someone looking for purpose in unlife.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Ish? I mean, Good Works are important, but Faith is considered more important by the vast majority. You can be a shit person, then repent on your deathbed, and still be saved.<br /> <br /> 3. Not to mention being bad for games. Good Works is a lot more active, which is better for stories!</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Would many atheist neonates really be interesting in finding a &quot;purpose in unlife&quot; if they didn't have those sort of concerns in life though?<br /> <br /> 2. In our school, we were taught that sincerity is integral to penance. If you truly focus on rejecting sin for good works, you're not a such shit person anymore. Whereas if you promise to never sin again <i>because</i> you'll never have the opportunity again, you're probably still a shit person. So Spears like Sylvia Baines in Chicago will interpret that by encouraging mortals to repent when for all they know, they will be able to do it again, before murdering them.<br /> <br /> 3. If the vampires are concerned with saving mortal souls, a belief in faith alone can be relevant and fun for the game. Some believers are pricks to say the least. The L&amp;S may well help those people against irreligious people who improve the lives of others if they think that it will strengthen the faith of the whole population. Maybe the pastor's corrupt, but by attracting more followers, the community's better off with him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T12:48:22-07:00","id":634956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634928#post634928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Would many atheist neonates really be interesting in finding a &quot;purpose in unlife&quot; if they didn't have those sort of concerns in life though?</div> </div> </div> </div> I know several atheist cops who joined the Force because they watned to something meaningful with their lives. Same idea, or at least that's what I'm trying to say. You don't need religion to have a purpose in life. That's the kind of person that could become an atheist Lance - drawn to the lifestyle, if not the beliefs.<br /> <br /> Plus, lets be honest. Theban Sorcery and magic powers is a pretty clear indication that there might very well be a God - many atheists are that because they don't see evidence of God. The supernatural have chances to come face to face with angels, qashmallim, and cherubim/seraphim. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. In our school, we were taught that sincerity is integral to penance. If you truly focus on rejecting sin for good works, you're not a such shit person anymore. Whereas if you promise to never sin again <i>because</i> you'll never have the opportunity again, you're probably still a shit person. So Spears like Sylvia Baines in Chicago will interpret that by encouraging mortals to repent when for all they know, they will be able to do it again, before murdering them. </div> </div> </div> I find that the history of the Church has put Faith Alone first in some times of its history, and sometimes less. It fluxuates, I think. I'm personally a Good Works woman myself, and constantly butt heads with the Faith people in my community. Either way, though, the Church kinda teaches both, so ignoring either is bad, according to the Church.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. If the vampires are concerned with saving mortal souls, a belief in faith alone can be relevant and fun for the game. Some believers are pricks to say the least. The L&amp;S may well help those people against irreligious people who improve the lives of others if they think that it will strengthen the faith of the whole population. Maybe the pastor's corrupt, but by attracting more followers, the community's better off with him. </div> </div> </div> I don't know if I'd say that they're concerned with saving mortal souls so much as punishing the wicked (and they can justify pretty much anyone as wicked), but in that spirit, you're right, its a <i>ton</i> of fun. And by scaring that corrupt preacher straight, you improve both his spirituality, and that of his flock as a whole.<br /> <br /> This is why the Lance have always remained my absolute favorite covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-21-2015, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:00:38-07:00","id":634983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625646-help-me-build-my-orthodox-ls?p=634871#post634871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ish? I mean, Good Works are important, but Faith is considered more important by the vast majority. You can be a shit person, then repent on your deathbed, and still be saved.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;I will repent on my death bed!&quot; is a famous cop-out, and advised against, may-not-work.<br /> Are you sincere, or are you repenting because you are batshit scared of going to hell? God knows.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. E